>
> We already have three sets of names of days of the week; why do we need a=
=20
> fourth? Though this set is obviously related to "nondei, pavdei, li'o".=
=20
> (Galician-Portuguese has two; I'm not aware of another natlang with more=
=20
> than=20
> one.)=20
>

It is for the same reason as {masnPA} proposal. Because of the definition=
=20
of {djedi}, lujvo ending with rafsi {-dei} signifies a full day, which is=
=20
duration, that is a length on time axis, not a date. In order to describe=
=20
unambiguously an event on a day of the week, we need a word for the day of=
=20
the week that inherit the place structure of {detri}, which signifies a=20
point on time axis.=20

We could make a lujvo like {jefydeipavdetri}, though I prefer a shorter=20
fu'ivla for convenience. If you don't like Stage-4 fu'ivla, you can use=20
lujvo {jefydeidetri} that I created for defining each fu'ivla of {jednPA}=
=20
series, as well as corresponding BAI {de'i'u}.=20

